WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.602 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We first met in this building
in 2001.

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:03.536 line:92%
You hosted my first "SNL",

00:00:03.536 --> 00:00:05.939
which was not the most memorable
part of that.

00:00:05.939 --> 00:00:08.375 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was also the first "SNL"
after 9/11,

00:00:08.375 --> 00:00:09.943 line:92%
which was a crazy "SNL" to host.

00:00:09.943 --> 00:00:10.744 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-Very burdensome.

00:00:10.744 --> 00:00:14.014
I will say, from my side it was
lovely to have somebody come in

00:00:14.014 --> 00:00:16.750
who was as sort of upbeat
and wonderful as you were.

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:19.786
-What you meant was as terrified
as you were.

00:00:19.786 --> 00:00:20.220 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:22.222 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I always felt bad for you,
because it was my --

00:00:22.222 --> 00:00:24.324 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was our --
both of our first "SNLs."

00:00:24.324 --> 00:00:25.959 align:start size:94% position:6%
I then, got to, like,
stick around

00:00:25.959 --> 00:00:28.828 size:84% position:42%
and do them as they got
farther away from 9/11.

00:00:28.828 --> 00:00:30.163 line:92%
But that's your only experience.

00:00:30.163 --> 00:00:32.232 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I waited 15 years
to come back.

00:00:32.232 --> 00:00:33.533 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, exactly.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:33.533 --> 00:00:36.202 align:start size:94% position:6%
That was very smart.
-I got really freaked out.

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:37.837 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-It was a lot of pressure.

00:00:37.837 --> 00:00:40.140 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I was really happy
to do it because --

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:41.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know Lorne
felt really strongly

00:00:41.608 --> 00:00:44.944
that the city needed to laugh
and that people needed to know

00:00:44.944 --> 00:00:47.280 align:start size:94% position:6%
that Americans
weren't going to be --

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:48.181 line:92%
we weren't gonna sit down

00:00:48.181 --> 00:00:50.817 align:start size:94% position:6%
and not let joy come back
into our lives.

00:00:50.817 --> 00:00:52.719 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And it was lovely,
because that was --

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:53.586 line:92%
I do feel like doing that show,

00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:55.422
everyone said,
"I'm so glad the show is back."

00:00:55.422 --> 00:00:57.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then like two weeks later
they were like,

00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:59.893 align:start size:94% position:6%
"This show sucks.
It was only good in the '70s."

00:00:59.893 --> 00:01:00.493 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:01.928
And that's when I really knew --
-That's not true.

00:01:01.928 --> 00:01:03.763 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's when I knew
that it was really back,

00:01:03.763 --> 00:01:05.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we were okay.
-You were amazing.

00:01:05.832 --> 00:01:06.399 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
You were so good.

00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:07.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I was not.
I was not fishing.

00:01:07.434 --> 00:01:10.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, congratulations
on this film.

00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:12.939 align:start size:94% position:6%
You had the premiere
the other night.

00:01:12.939 --> 00:01:13.373 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:01:13.373 --> 00:01:14.941 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Was this a book that you were
familiar with?

00:01:14.941 --> 00:01:18.778
-Yes. I read this book when I
was 12 and I just loved it.

00:01:18.778 --> 00:01:19.546 size:75% position:38% line:92%
"A Wrinkle in Time."

00:01:19.546 --> 00:01:21.448 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I read every book
in the series,

00:01:21.448 --> 00:01:24.350 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I was also
a little bit of a nerd.

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:24.884 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.884 --> 00:01:26.486 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I just thought
it was magical.

00:01:26.486 --> 00:01:28.555 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was -- I loved sci-fi
as a little girl,

00:01:28.555 --> 00:01:31.424 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I didn't always find books
that had a girl

00:01:31.424 --> 00:01:34.094 line:92%
at the center of a sci-fi story.

00:01:34.094 --> 00:01:34.828 line:92%
So it was really exciting.

00:01:34.828 --> 00:01:36.963
And my kids read the book, too,
in sixth grade.

00:01:36.963 --> 00:01:40.633
-And were they excited when you
get cast in a book they've read?

00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:41.868 line:92%
-Yeah. They were really excited.

00:01:41.868 --> 00:01:43.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I said to my son,
I said, well --

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:46.606
because I couldn't really
remember what the character was.

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:48.741
I said, "Well, Ava DuVernay just
called me

00:01:48.741 --> 00:01:50.176 align:start size:94% position:6%
and asked me
if I'd be Mrs. Whatsit."

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:56.349
And he's like, "Mrs. Whatsit's
like a really, really old lady."

00:01:56.349 --> 00:01:57.417 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.417 --> 00:01:58.818 line:92%
And I was like, "Really?"

00:01:58.818 --> 00:02:02.188
So I called my agent and I go,
"She wants me to play like a --

00:02:02.188 --> 00:02:06.226
I know, I mean, I'm over 40 in
Hollywood but, I mean, really?"

00:02:06.226 --> 00:02:06.793 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.793 --> 00:02:07.760 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Like a really old lady?

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:10.163 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so anyway,
she said, "No, no, no.

00:02:10.163 --> 00:02:10.830 size:81% position:41% line:92%
I want to reimagine it

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:13.733 align:start size:94% position:6%
as these incredible celestial
beings who are funny."

00:02:13.733 --> 00:02:16.736
And I was like, "Oh. Okay, yeah.
Okay, cool."

00:02:16.736 --> 00:02:17.337 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.337 --> 00:02:18.037 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Oh, cool. Yeah, yeah.

00:02:18.037 --> 00:02:21.741
-Good, 'cause I also saw myself
as more of a celestial being.

00:02:21.741 --> 00:02:22.342 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.342 --> 00:02:23.042 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Yeah. Less old lady.

00:02:23.042 --> 00:02:25.945 size:81% position:41%
Like, more like a star
fallen from the sky.

00:02:25.945 --> 00:02:26.479 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.479 --> 00:02:28.014 line:92%
-You have incredible co-stars.

00:02:28.014 --> 00:02:29.215 line:92%
Mindy Kaling is one of them,

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:31.384 align:start size:94% position:6%
who I adore
and she's just wonderful.

00:02:31.384 --> 00:02:32.919 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Love Mindy.
-Just the best.

00:02:32.919 --> 00:02:34.554 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
-You guys!

00:02:34.554 --> 00:02:37.090 align:start size:94% position:6%
Mindy Kaling, we would, like,
joke on the set because,

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:38.691 align:start size:94% position:6%
it was like me, Oprah,
and Mindy Kaling.

00:02:38.691 --> 00:02:41.327
And, like, every time Mindy
would walk out the door,

00:02:41.327 --> 00:02:42.262 line:92%
she'd come back, she'd be like,

00:02:42.262 --> 00:02:44.230
"Well, I re-wrote a script
and I also did a podcast

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:47.400
and I also wrote my new episode
of my new television show."

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:48.234 line:92%
I was like, "I mean, what?"

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:50.236 size:84% position:42%
And then Oprah would be
over there going, like,

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:52.572 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I have to do a board meeting
on the phone.

00:02:52.572 --> 00:02:53.273 size:81% position:41% line:92%
Can you guys be quiet?

00:02:53.273 --> 00:02:55.842 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm also finding a new C.E.O.
for Weight Watchers.

00:02:55.842 --> 00:02:56.376 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And also --"

00:02:56.376 --> 00:02:58.278
And I was, like, "I got to step
up my game, you guys."

00:02:58.278 --> 00:02:59.946 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-How was -- Well, you --

00:02:59.946 --> 00:03:01.514 size:81% position:41%
I mean, you have been
stepping up your game.

00:03:01.514 --> 00:03:04.250
You're selling yourself short,
because you've been producing --

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:06.619 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, 'cause I've got to keep
up with Mindy and Oprah!

00:03:06.619 --> 00:03:08.755
-Yeah, that's true.
That's a very unfair bar to set.

00:03:08.755 --> 00:03:11.491 align:start size:94% position:6%
How but -- Real quick,
how is it to be around Oprah?

00:03:11.491 --> 00:03:12.392 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's amazing.
-Yeah.

00:03:12.392 --> 00:03:15.562 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I can't actually believe they
paid me American dollars

00:03:15.562 --> 00:03:18.097 align:start size:94% position:6%
to get to sit next to her
and learn every --

00:03:18.097 --> 00:03:20.266 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, she's just --
I was scared, too.

00:03:20.266 --> 00:03:22.802
Because, you know, sometimes you
meet your heroes

00:03:22.802 --> 00:03:26.039 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they're not as awesome
as you want them to be.

00:03:26.039 --> 00:03:28.675 line:92%
She's better than I imagined.

00:03:28.675 --> 00:03:30.443 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I once sat next to her
at a restaurant,

00:03:30.443 --> 00:03:32.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I so wanted to go over
and say hi,

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:33.279 size:88% position:44% line:92%
but then I also thought,

00:03:33.279 --> 00:03:35.281 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think Oprah more than anyone
deserves a quiet meal.

00:03:35.281 --> 00:03:37.550
And then I shifted from not only
was I not gonna say hi,

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:41.020
but if anyone approached the
table I'd take a swing at them.

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:41.554 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:41.554 --> 00:03:43.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, "You leave this woman
alone!"

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:44.924 line:92%
-"She's an American treasure!"

00:03:44.924 --> 00:03:45.858 line:92%
-"She's done so much for you!"

00:03:45.858 --> 00:03:49.429
-Oh, see, I go the other way and
go, "Want to be best friends?"

00:03:49.429 --> 00:03:51.231 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, right.
Well, that would work.

00:03:51.231 --> 00:03:53.266 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"I'm really fun at parties."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:53.266 --> 00:03:55.902
-But again, you are -- you also
have been so prolific.

00:03:55.902 --> 00:03:59.539
You've been producing shows.
You produced "Big Little Lies."

00:03:59.539 --> 00:04:01.574 align:start size:94% position:6%
Congratulations.
-Yes. Thank you.

00:04:01.574 --> 00:04:02.709 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:02.709 --> 00:04:05.011 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know -- Obviously this is
one of those shows

00:04:05.011 --> 00:04:06.346 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you can't talk
too much about,

00:04:06.346 --> 00:04:09.315
but certainly season two has
some very exciting casting news.

00:04:09.315 --> 00:04:10.984 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, y'all,
we're starting next Friday

00:04:10.984 --> 00:04:15.188
on "Big Little Lies" two.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:15.188 --> 00:04:15.855 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I can't believe it.

00:04:15.855 --> 00:04:18.825 align:start size:94% position:6%
And not only do we have
every cast member coming back,

00:04:18.825 --> 00:04:21.261 align:start size:94% position:6%
but also Meryl Streep
is joining us.

00:04:21.261 --> 00:04:24.163 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:24.163 --> 00:04:24.831 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-What is that like?

00:04:24.831 --> 00:04:27.867 align:start size:94% position:6%
What is the moment
where you get Meryl Streep

00:04:27.867 --> 00:04:29.002 line:92%
to agree to do your show?

00:04:29.002 --> 00:04:31.204 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, she sent an e-mail
to Nicole and I.

00:04:31.204 --> 00:04:34.173 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it said, "Okay, I read
the part and I love it

00:04:34.173 --> 00:04:35.141 size:88% position:44% line:92%
and I'm going to do it."

00:04:35.141 --> 00:04:36.509 line:92%
And I, like, dropped the phone.

00:04:36.509 --> 00:04:38.811 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, mike drop,
but I phone-dropped.

00:04:38.811 --> 00:04:39.379 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And I was like --

00:04:39.379 --> 00:04:42.315
and then I called Nicole and I
was like, "Is this real life?

00:04:42.315 --> 00:04:43.449 line:92%
Like, is this really happening?"

00:04:43.449 --> 00:04:45.351 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then I got off the phone
with Nicole

00:04:45.351 --> 00:04:48.221 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I, like, hugged myself
gently for a minute.

00:04:48.221 --> 00:04:48.755 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:48.755 --> 00:04:50.023 align:start size:94% position:6%
And said,
"This is really happening.

00:04:50.023 --> 00:04:52.025 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're really working with
Meryl Streep."

00:04:52.025 --> 00:04:53.559 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then I called the writer
and go,

00:04:53.559 --> 00:04:56.629
"You better write me good scenes
with Meryl Streep!"

00:04:56.629 --> 00:04:57.163 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:57.163 --> 00:04:58.665 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do you think Meryl Streep,
historically,

00:04:58.665 --> 00:05:00.600 size:75% position:38%
every time she said,
"I'll do the part"

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:03.102 align:start size:94% position:6%
has then -- hears a phone
hit the ground?

00:05:03.102 --> 00:05:03.636 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:03.636 --> 00:05:05.038 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, that's just
what she goes through.

00:05:05.038 --> 00:05:07.640
-Or, like, just somebody falling
over like --

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:08.308 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Light laughter ]

00:05:08.308 --> 00:05:09.742 align:start size:94% position:6%
-She says,
"I have some news for you,

00:05:09.742 --> 00:05:12.111 size:88% position:44%
but I want to make sure
you're near a hospital."

00:05:12.111 --> 00:05:13.746 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
"Are you sitting down?"

00:05:13.746 --> 00:05:15.181 line:92%
-Well, congratulations on that.

00:05:15.181 --> 00:05:16.582 line:92%
I am so excited to watch it.

00:05:16.582 --> 00:05:17.317 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Congrats on the movie

00:05:17.317 --> 00:05:19.118
and it's always such a pleasure
to see you.

00:05:19.118 --> 00:05:21.387 size:81% position:41%
Thanks for being here.
-So nice to see you.

